			"date": "2023-12-12T19:01:18.000Z",
			"content": "<p><span class=\"h-card\" translate=\"no\"><a href=\"https://fediverse.zachleat.com/@zachleat\" class=\"u-url mention\" rel=\"nofollow noopener\" target=\"_blank\">@<span>zachleat</span></a></span> The idea that one 'youtube embed weighs 1.2 MB' reminds me of something I heard years ago. A government project required developing software going into an airplane. \"What does it weight?\" \"Huh?\" \"Everything in an airplane has to specify a weight.\" So, they listed the weight of a floppy disk. This caused a major complaint: \"You are way out of line on the price per pound ratio.\"  Finally they explained it as \"tooling costs.\"</p>",
